difftest-firmware: add the difftest_set_firmware_* entry points the harness calls

Classification: harness plumbing.

The MSSIM platform signals TPM_SET_FW_HASH and TPM_SET_FW_SVN carry a value
(the simulator's TcpServer reads it and calls _rpc__SetTpmFirmwareHash() /
_rpc__SetTpmFirmwareSvn()). The differential harness delivers them through
these entry points, which call the platform functions directly
(_plat__SetTpmFirmwareHash() / _plat__SetTpmFirmwareSvn(), which caps the
SVN at MAX_SVN), whatever the power state, like the simulator. They change
the Firmware Secret and the current firmware SVN of the firmware-limited and
SVN-limited hierarchies (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "TPM Firmware-Limited and
SVN-Limited Objects"). The harness also calls them after every
re-initialization, so that a re-initialized reference starts with the
firmware of a new process (hash FIRMWARE_V2, SVN 10).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/Simulator/src/TPMCmdp.c b/TPMCmd/Simulator/src/TPMCmdp.c
--- a/TPMCmd/Simulator/src/TPMCmdp.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/Simulator/src/TPMCmdp.c
@@ -224,6 +224,18 @@ bool _rpc__ACT_GetSignaled(uint32_t actHandle)
     return false;
 }
 
+//*** tpm-rs differential testing firmware entry points
+
+void difftest_set_firmware_hash(uint32_t hash)
+{
+    _plat__SetTpmFirmwareHash(hash);
+}
+
+void difftest_set_firmware_svn(uint16_t svn)
+{
+    _plat__SetTpmFirmwareSvn(svn);
+}
+
 //*** _rpc__SetTpmFirmwareHash()
 // This function is used to modify the firmware's hash during simulation.
 void _rpc__SetTpmFirmwareHash(uint32_t hash)
